    "summary": "Epic He Was A Friend Of Mine, Dark Star & tight set flow",
    "blurb": "The show delivers a soaring He Was A Friend Of Mine and a marathon Dark Star that keep the energy high throughout. Jerry’s lead work shines on the ballads while the band locks into The Other One and Turn On Your Lovelight. Overall the performance is solid with standout moments across both sets.",
    "review": "On May 31, 1969 at McArthur Court in Eugene, the Dead served up a classic late‑'60s marathon that still feels fresh. The first set builds from tight R&B numbers into an improvisational surge highlighted by a seamless transition into The Other One, followed by a soulful rendition of Sittin’ On Top Of The World and a gritty It Hurts Me Too before the crowd‑pleasing Turn On Your Lovelight. Set two kicks off with an emotionally charged He Was A Friend Of Mine that segues into one of the era’s most compelling Dark Star journeys—long, exploratory, and full of Jerry’s soaring leads. The encore closes on the haunting Baby Blue cover, leaving a lingering sense of wonder. Across both soundboard sources the playing is consistently strong; the Oleynick capture offers the clearest mix with only minor drop‑outs, making it the preferred listening version.",
